status: enforce_1_2
exit: 0
note: |
  Form C. `main` nested INSIDE `place Entry { }`. The compiler accepts this today
  (it compiles and runs, exit 0), but it is a deviation: `place Entry` is a marker,
  `main` belongs at the top level, and every one of the 34 examples/ projects keeps
  it there. This is the form that bit us on 2026-07-02 (a fix-pass silently moved
  mains inside `place Entry`, diverging the book from the corpus with no compiler
  signal). It is registered here as a debt.

  The gate compiles it and asserts it still passes today, so the ledger never lies
  about the current state. When enforcement lands in 1.2 (the checker rejecting a
  nested main), this fixture will START to fail compilation, and THAT failure is the
  cue to flip `status` to reject_clean and add the `match` fragment of the new error.
  At that moment this file becomes the acceptance test for the 1.2 fix.
